# Kindred Local Events Discovery Engine

Kindred is not trying to list every event. Kindred discovers the **best**
events before anyone else and presents them in a calm, beautiful newspaper.

The reader goal: *"I had no idea this was happening near me."*

## Trusted source network

Build connectors for official and semi-official sources — city calendars,
parks & recreation, libraries, museums, tourism bureaus, universities, NPS,
Eventbrite, Ticketmaster, AXS, Fever, and official venue websites.

Registry: `supabase/functions/_shared/localEvents/sources/types.ts`

Active connectors expand over time; inactive sources are documented for future wiring.

## Editorial pipeline (every edition build)

1. Gather from all enabled connectors
2. Remove duplicates (prefer official > venue > aggregator)
3. Normalize dates, URLs, and provenance
4. Rank by editorial quality and relevance — not raw popularity
5. Publish events meeting the quality threshold

Orchestrator: `supabase/functions/_shared/localEvents/pipeline.ts`

## Editorial ranking favors

Unique, seasonal, family-friendly, community-focused, free, educational,
visually interesting, outdoor-suitable (weather-aware), and worth driving to.

Do not rank by popularity alone. Think like an experienced newspaper editor.

## Images

Prefer authentic listing photography from providers. Never invent facts from photos.
Genre fallbacks on the client are last resort only when the provider supplies nothing.

